     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. I need you to confirm the dose first.\n\n**Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is 5 times the maximum recommended dose.** The usual adult dose is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and 10 mg/day is the most it's labeled for. At 50 mg, the patient is at risk of severe low blood pressure, reflex tachycardia, swelling, and amlodipine overdose. Amlodipine overdose is hard to reverse because the drug stays in the body for a long time (half-life of about 30\u201350 hours).\n\nThis looks like it could be a typo for **5 mg**, which is a common starting dose. Can you tell me which you meant?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**\n2. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily** (the maximum)\n3. **Another dose.** If you really do intend more than 10 mg/day, tell me the clinical reason and I'll add it as a note on the order.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
     ],
