      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I entered the order as you confirmed: **amlodipine 50 mg PO once daily (ORD-0001)**.\n\nThe order carries a note saying the dose is 5 times the maximum labeled dose, that you were warned and confirmed it as written, and that no clinical reason was given. It also asks pharmacy to verify before dispensing, so pharmacy may contact you.\n\nIf you meant 5 mg, tell me and I'll enter the corrected order. You'd need to cancel ORD-0001, since I can't cancel orders with the tools I have. If 50 mg is intended, please keep a close eye on the patient. Watch for low blood pressure, especially after the first dose, and for tachycardia and swelling. Amlodipine lasts a long time in the body, so any toxicity could last for days."
